{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And I will cut off</b> — that they had no horse when they were under the dominion of Greece." "<b>And the meaning of \"from Ephraim\"</b> — these are those who come from Assyria, as I explained, and he said concerning this king, that at the end he will speak peace to the nations." "<b>And his dominion</b> — his rule from the Sea of Reeds to the sea of the Philistines." "<b>And from the River</b> — the Euphrates." "<b>To the ends of the earth</b> — this is the wilderness. \"Peace to the nations,\" and this is the border of the land of Israel. Also he said at the beginning concerning this king that he is righteous and therefore he is helped, and he returned and spoke to Israel."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {4 "The phrase 'הוא המדבר שלום לגוים' is textually difficult; read hyper-literally as 'it is the wilderness, peace to the nations,' though the textual division between gloss and citation is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:31.967781574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}